---
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
const { c, index } = Astro.props;
const d = c.data;
const file = c.id === 'exfil' ? 'transfer' : c.id === 'benign' ? 'benign-transfer' : c.id;
---
<article class="proof-case" id={c.id}>
  <header class="case-heading"><span class="pill">CASE 0{index + 1} / {c.label}</span><h2>{c.title}</h2><p class="case-scenario">{c.scenario}</p><div class="case-meta"><span>Saved run: <code>{d.bundle}</code></span><span>Completion: <code>{d.completion}</code></span></div></header>
  <div class="record-comparison">
    <section class="record-pane"><div class="record-title"><span class="eyebrow">SURICATA → SIEM</span><h3>{c.left}</h3><p>Selected {d.suricata.event_type} record · original exported document body</p></div><div class="record-code" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${c.label}: Suricata record`}><Code code={JSON.stringify(d.suricata,null,2)} lang="json" theme="github-dark" /></div></section>
    <section class="record-pane"><div class="record-title"><span class="eyebrow">SURICATA → CERNITY → SIEM</span><h3>{c.right}</h3><p>Selected finding · original exported document body</p></div><div class="record-code" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={`${c.label}: Cernity record`}><Code code={JSON.stringify(d.cernity,null,2)} lang="json" theme="github-dark" /></div></section>
  </div>
  <div class="record-caption">These are complete selected document bodies from saved SIEM exports, pretty-printed without changing values. The escaped <code>entities</code> string is preserved exactly as a string. Search-result wrappers such as an Elasticsearch <code>_index</code> or <code>_id</code> were not retained in these exports and are not reconstructed here.</div>
  <details class="source-records"><summary>Read a simplified view with decoded entities</summary><div class="record-comparison"><div class="record-code" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Simplified Suricata document"><Code code={JSON.stringify(d.suricata_excerpt,null,2)} lang="json" theme="github-dark" /></div><div class="record-code" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Cernity document with decoded entities"><Code code={JSON.stringify(d.cernity_excerpt,null,2)} lang="json" theme="github-dark" /></div></div><p>All {d.cernity_matching_records.length} matching Cernity documents are included in the download, including distinct IDs and revisions.</p></details>
  {d.additional_alert && c.id !== 'signature' && <details class="source-records"><summary>Inspect a Suricata stream-anomaly alert from this pair</summary><div class="record-code" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Suricata stream anomaly alert"><Code code={JSON.stringify(d.additional_alert,null,2)} lang="json" theme="github-dark" /></div></details>}
  <section class="case-explanation"><span class="eyebrow">WHAT CERNITY ADDED</span><p>{c.change}</p></section>
  <div class="case-reading"><section><h3>Read the records</h3><dl>{c.read.map(([field,meaning])=><div><dt>{field}</dt><dd>{meaning}</dd></div>)}</dl></section><aside class="analyst-notes"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR NEXT INVESTIGATION</span><h3>What would you check?</h3><ol>{c.investigation.map(step=><li>{step}</li>)}</ol><details class="knowledge-check"><summary>{c.question}</summary><p>{c.answer}</p></details></aside></div>
  <div class="case-limit"><strong>What this does not establish</strong><p>{c.limit}</p></div>
  <div class="case-download"><a class="text-link" href={`/evidence/${file}.json`} download>Download selected records and verification metadata ↓</a><a href="#methodology">How these records were verified →</a></div>
</article>
